# A patch file's whitespace is the patched project's, not this one's.
#
# A patch against a tab-indented C tree carries context lines from that tree,
# and a diff prefixes every context line with a space, so every one of them
# reads as "space before tab in indent" to `git diff --check`. Reindenting them
# would stop the patch applying, which is the one thing it has to do.
*.patch -whitespace
*.diff -whitespace

# A PlayStation boot descriptor's line endings are the console's, not this
# repository's. SYSTEM.CNF goes onto the disc byte for byte, and the convention
# every pressed disc follows is CRLF. The carriage returns are content, not
# trailing whitespace, and no checkout may convert them away.
platform/playstation/disc/SYSTEM.CNF -whitespace -text
